{"content":[{"c":["SALLU"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Son of Meshullam and a Benjaminite, who resided in the city of Jerusalem during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.7","r":"1Chr.9.7","rawR":"1Chr.9.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.7","value":"1Chr.9.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.7","r":"Neh.11.7","rawR":"Neh.11.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.7","value":"Neh.11.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levitical priest who returned to Jerusalem with Zerubbabel following the Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.7","r":"Neh.12.7","rawR":"Neh.12.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.7","value":"Neh.12.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:7"},"). The Sallai mentioned in some translations of ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.20","r":"Neh.12.20","rawR":"Neh.12.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.20","value":"Neh.12.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 12:20"}," is thought to be a variant spelling of Sallu."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Sallu","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.7"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.7","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.7","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.7"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.7","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.7","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.7"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 12:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.20","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.20","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ccfac619309b567d6f9d8b067c778c8730a52c4ea757052080eec0526c80e44f","sou